<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Bolsena</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsena">Bolsena</a> is a crater lake in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazio">Lazio</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, the largest lake of volcanic origin in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. In Etruscan times its shores belonged to the territory of Volsinii, and the federal sanctuary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fanum-voltumnae">Fanum Voltumnae</a>, lay nearby. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> the commune of Orvieto extended its rule towards it, and the Farnese Duchy of Castro later covered the lands between the lake and the Tyrrhenian coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-bolsena.jpg" alt="Lake Bolsena" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Jackyd101 assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Bolsena_from_Montefiascone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
